  "description": "Speed Without Sacrifice\nInspired by the medieval Scottish two-handed great sword, known for its strength and symbolism of the rugged Highlands, Deviate’s award-winning Claymore embodies this legacy - crafted to conquer the world's most challenging terrains. Now available in a new range of colours inspired by Scotland’s heritage, this long-travel enduro bike is as striking as it is capable.\nThe 2026 Claymore Factory is built for one thing: getting you down the hill faster, smoother, and with fewer stops at the tool bench. 165mm rear travel, a 180mm fork, and a high-pivot layout that stays composed in chaos. Point it down anything.\nEvery part on this build is race-ready. The new FOX 38 GRIP X2 and Float X2 Factory suspension offers improved traction, support, and tuneability. The wireless Shimano XTR/XT Di2 drivetrain delivers flawless shifting—no cables, no compromise. Braking comes from Shimano XTR 4-pistons, with a 220mm front rotor for maximum control under pressure.\nWe’ve spec’d Reserve HD alloy wheels laced to ONEUP hubs, with Continental Kryptotal Enduro SuperSoft (front) and Downhill Soft (rear) tires. These won’t flinch in a rock garden or a week-long stage race.",
